<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.6.3: Connecting Graphical and Verbal Representations of a Function</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00945</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.6.3: Connecting Graphical and Verbal Representations of a Function</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e0155615-2551-450a-ab87-00f63a493175</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity </title>
<para>In a bungee jump, the height of the jumper is a function of time since the jump begins.</para>
<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
  <!-- Graph Cell -->
  <div class="graph-cell">
    <para><figure><media alt="Graph of curve. Horizontal axis, 0 to 35 by 5’s, t, seconds. Vertical axis, 0 to 90 by 10’s, h, meters. Curve starts a 0 comma 80, decreases then increases, 4 times."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7659f784a4274c607be52c4e74b48d39b3546cc2"/></media></figure></para>
  </div>
  <!-- Expressions and Equations Cell -->
  <div class="expressions-cell">
    <para>Expressions and Equations:</para>
    <list>
      <item>\(h(0)\)</item>
      <item>\(h(t)=0\)</item>
      <item>\(h(4)\)</item>
      <item>\(h(t)=80\)</item>
      <item>\(h(t)=45\)</item>
    </list>
  </div>
  <!-- Features Cell -->
  <div class="features-cell">
    <para>Features:</para>
    <list>
      <item>first dip in the graph</item>
      <item>vertical intercept</item>
      <item>first peak in the graph</item>
      <item>horizontal intercept</item>
      <item>maximum</item>
    </list>
  </div>
</div>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Match each description about the jump to a corresponding expression or equation and to a feature on the graph.</item>
</list>
<para>One expression or equation does not have a matching verbal description. Its corresponding graphical feature is also not shown on the graph. Interpret that expression or equation in terms of the jump and in terms of the graph of the function. Record your interpretation in the last row of the table.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>Description of Jump</para>
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>Expression or Equation</para>
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>Feature of Graph</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
          <item>the greatest height that the jumper is from the river</item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
          <item>the height from which the jumper was jumping</item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
          <item>the time at which the jumper reached the highest point after the first bounce</item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
          <item>the lowest point that the jumper reached in the entire jump</item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
          <item>the time at which the jumper hits the surface of the river</item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Expression or Equation</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(h(t)=80\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
